---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import DefaultLayout from '../../../layouts/DefaultLayout.astro';

const projects = await getCollection('projects_en');
const omicsApps = projects.filter(p => p.data.category === 'omics');
const cncProjects = projects.filter(p => p.data.category === 'cnc');
---

<DefaultLayout title="Projects" lang="en">
  <h1>Here are my projects</h1>

  <h2>OmicsVerse</h2>

  <video autoplay loop muted playsinline disablepictureinpicture disableremoteplayback style="max-width: 100%; height: auto">
    <source src="/portfolio/Omicsverse.webm" type="video/webm" />
  </video>

  <p>The initial aim of the <a href="https://omicsverse.fr">OmicsVerse portal</a> is to host demo versions of the various data applications I create.</p>
  <p>The databases are built from nf-core pipeline outputs: data engineering and modeling, user training.</p>
  <p>Application source code and documentation for administrators can be found on my <a href="https://github.com/clbenoit">github</a>.</p>
  <p>The following sections &amp; pages will host detailed documentation of users.</p>
  <p>If you have a genomics-oriented data application to host, don't hesitate to contact me, provided there are resources available.</p>

  <ul>
    {omicsApps.map(p => (
      <li>
        <a href={`/portfolio/en/projects/${p.id}/`}>{p.data.title}</a>
        {p.data.description && (
          <div class="project-list-desc">{p.data.description}</div>
        )}
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <h3>Can I use it for clinical purposes?</h3>

  <p>The honest answer is: <b>not yet</b>.</p>
  <p>These are <b>research and exploratory tools</b>.<br />
  Using it in routine diagnostics would require compliance with<br />
  medical device software regulations and formal validation processes
  <a href="/portfolio/en/projects/#ref-1">[1]</a> <a href="/portfolio/en/projects/#ref-2">[2]</a> <a href="/portfolio/en/projects/#ref-3">[3]</a>.</p>
  <p>This is far beyond what a single developer can realistically achieve alone.<br /><br />
  So if you feel like contributing to the project, don't hesitate to contact me:
  <a href="mailto:benoitclement.data@gmail.com">benoitclement.data@gmail.com</a>.</p>
  <p>That said, these tools are designed to <b>lower the barrier</b> for institutions that want to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Reclaim control over their methylation data.</li>
    <li>Prepare internal validation efforts.</li>
    <li>Build collective expertise instead of outsourcing it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>CNC Collective</h2>

  <p><b>CNC (Chartreuse Node Crew)</b> is a 6+ developer collective (Grenoble, Paris, decentralized) that I co-founded, providing cross-functional coordination and technical leadership: scalable architecture, code review, prioritization and time-to-market optimization. The collective develops and operates in production for its members a <b>sovereign self-hosted AI infrastructure</b> (LLM/ML model serving, agentic workflows), <b>cloud services</b> and a <b>development platform</b> (agentic harness). Before this pivot, it provided a liquid staking service for two years (2024 – 2025): ~90% of its members exited in gains.</p>

  <ul>
    {cncProjects.map(p => (
      <li>
        <a href={`/portfolio/en/projects/${p.id}/`}>{p.data.title}</a>
        {p.data.description && (
          <div class="project-list-desc">{p.data.description}</div>
        )}
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <h2>References</h2>

  <p id="ref-1">
    <b>[1]</b> Tuomas Granlund; Tommi Mikkonen; Vlad Stirbu (2020).<br />
    <i>On Medical Device Software CE Compliance and Conformity Assessment</i>.<br />
    <b>IEEE</b>.<br />
    <a href="https://doi.org/10.1109/ICSA-C50368.2020.00040" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">DOI</a>
  </p>
  <p id="ref-2">
    <b>[2]</b> Cyrille Michaud (2020).<br />
    <i>How to qualify, classify and CE mark software</i>.<br />
    <b>MD101</b>.<br />
    <a href="https://blog.cm-dm.com/pages/How-to-qualify%2C-classify-and-CE-mark-software" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">URL</a>
  </p>
  <p id="ref-3">
    <b>[3]</b> Małgorzata Kruszynska (2021).<br />
    <i>CE marking for Medical Device Software: a step-by-step guide</i>.<br />
    <b>Spyrosoft</b>.<br />
    <a href="https://spyro-soft.com/blog/healthcare/ce-marking-for-medical-device-software" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">URL</a>
  </p>
</DefaultLayout>

<style>
  .project-list-desc {
    color: var(--color-text3);
    font-size: 0.9em;
    margin-top: 2px;
  }
</style>
